# What does NOT get uploaded to Vercel.
#
# The moment this file exists, .gitignore stops being consulted — so anything
# that must stay off the build machine has to be named here, including the
# things .gitignore already covers. That is the trap in this file.
#
# Keep `certs/` OUT of this list. certs/supabase-ca.crt is what makes the
# database connection verify who it is talking to; without it the connection
# still works and is still encrypted, so its absence is invisible.
# See docs/project/database.md and certs/README.md.

.git
node_modules

# Secrets. Production values live in the Vercel project's environment settings,
# never in a file that gets uploaded.
#
# `.env*`, matching .gitignore exactly, and NOT the narrower `.env` + `.env.*`
# this used to say — that pair misses `.envrc` and `.env-production`, so the
# first person to add one would upload it without anything saying so. GPT Sol
# found it in review, 2026-08-26.
.env*
!.env.example

# Built here, not shipped from here. api-dist is the compiled API — see
# vite.api.config.ts — and a stale local copy must never win over a fresh build.
dist
api-dist

# Articles on this laptop. Production reads them out of Postgres.
data
output

# Nothing in the build or the deployed function reads any of these — a claim
# this file makes and cannot check. The `build` gate in scripts/deploy.ts is
# what checks it: it renames these aside before building, because reaching into
# one of them resolves everywhere except on Vercel. See
# docs/postmortems/260907a-an-import-into-a-vercelignored-directory-built-everywhere-except-vercel.md
#
# (The local dev server is a deliberate exception — vite.config.ts reads
# supabase/config.toml in an `apply: "serve"` plugin, which never ships.)
docs
evals
tests
example
supabase
scratch-*
